+# Phase 8 Plan 02: Workspace Package Rename to the @hestia Scope Summary
+
+**All seven workspace packages are now `@hestia/*` and the root is `hestia`, with a pnpm-generated lockfile that changed only six importer keys and a service bundle that still inlines every workspace package.**
+
+## Performance
+
+- **Duration:** about 7 min (start 2026-10-26T03:26:48Z; the SUMMARY was written at about 03:34Z)
+- **Tasks:** 2
+- **Files modified:** 216 across the two commits (including the two new phase files)
+
+## Accomplishments
+
+- One scripted substitution (`@hearth(\\?/)` to `@hestia\1`) over the class selector renamed 212 files, covering plain imports, the regex literal in `apps/service/tsup.config.ts` and `scripts/test-sweep.test.mjs`, and the `@hearth/${workspace}` templates in `scripts/test-sweep.mjs`. The root `"name"` line was changed separately.
+- `.planning/environment/cloud-setup.sh` lines 122 and 129 were edited by hand (root-name probe and the Playwright filter); no other line of that file was touched.
+- `pnpm install --lockfile-only` (online) rewrote exactly the six importer keys. `pnpm install --frozen-lockfile --offline` accepted it and relinked; no `@hearth` entry remains under any `node_modules`.
+- `pnpm --filter @hestia/service build` succeeded and no `apps/service/dist/*.js` file has an `@hestia/` import specifier, so the pruned production install in the Dockerfile needs no workspace source. The web build and `check-build.mjs` passed (app shell 198.2 KB gzipped against a 200 KB budget).
+- Phase copy of the docs-claims checker and allowlist added; the archive under `.planning/milestones/` is identical to the planning commit `d544a3b`.
+
